  "summary": "Recent preprints pair likelihood-free inference tutorials and head-to-head comparisons with mechanistic epidemic models.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is inference for mechanistic epidemic models whose likelihoods are hard to evaluate directly. Simulation-based routes dominate the inference-focused items: an ABC-SMC tutorial in PyMC for ecological and epidemiological models, neural posterior estimation for Ebola epidemiological and phylodynamic models with online tutorials, and a comparison of particle MCMC against conditional normalizing flows for stochastic SIS, SIR and SEIR models. Other items apply learning or statistical frameworks to new data types: a semi-supervised deep network estimating COVID-19 daily case counts from wastewater viral RNA, a phylogeny-free framework profiling source-sink mutation dynamics across 6.6M SARS-CoV-2 genomes, and a perturbation-augmented neural ODE for gut microbiome dynamics. What is new is the pairing of specific data structures with specific inference or modeling tools, a pattern not shared by every item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-12-02"
}
